<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diplomatic marriage</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as dynastic marriages, diplomatic marriages</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diplomatic marriage is the practice of arranging royal marriages to seal alliances between states. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a> made extensive use of it, sending princesses to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, as recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>. Such marriages reinforced the peace between Mitanni and Egypt and formed part of the diplomatic system of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>.</p></div>
